scale invariant valuation. The uniform rate of deletion in the case of a measure zero set is violated because of the underlying reparametrisation invariance. Further, in a dynamical process leading to a Cantor set, a positive measure Cantor set $C_p$ is favoured a.s (almost surely) compared to a measure zero set $C_{\alpha}$ since relative infinitesimal neighbours a.s. lie in a Cantor set $C_{\alpha^{\prime}}$ satisfying the above constraints.

