Suppose that~\eqref{eq:alg_curv_tensor_1}-\eqref{eq:alg_curv_tensor_2} hold for a pair $(\kappa,C)$ and that $\dim(M)\geq 2$. We show that the cyclic sum $\cyclic_{xyz} 
abla_x\kappa(y,z)$ vanishes at each point $p\in M$. We distinguish two cases: If there exists an open neighbourhood around $p$ where $	race \, \kappa$ is constant, then $\kappa$ is Killing on this neighbourhood according to~\eqref{eq:zweite_vorstufe_zur_Bianchi_identity}. Suppose there exists a point $p\in M$ such that $\d \, 	race \, \kappa|_p
eq 0$. In particular, $\kappa$ is not a constant multiple of the metric tensor on any open neighbourhood of $p$. Therefore each neighbourhood of $p$ in $M$ is irreducible according to Lemma~ef{le:M_is_irreducible}. Hence we can assume that $M$ is simply connected and irreducible. Further, recall that the cyclic sum $\cyclic_{xyz}
abla_x\kappa(y,z)$ is a parallel symmetric 3-tensor according to Lemma~ef{le:Bianchis_cyclic_sum_is_parallel}. Therefore if the holonomy group of $M$ at $p$ acts transitively on the unit sphere of $T_pM$, then the corresponding homogeneous polynomial function $f(x) := 
abla_x\kappa(x,x)$ with $x\in T_pM$ is constant on vectors of equal length. Since the degree of $f$ is odd, we see that $f(x) = f(-x) = - f(x)$ for all $x\in T_pM$ . Therefore $\cyclic_{xyz} 
abla_x\kappa(y,z)|_p = 0$. If, by contradiction, we assume that the holonomy group acts non-transitively, then $M$ is locally symmetric, $
abla R = 0$, according to Bergers classification of holonomy groups~\cite[5.21]{Ba}. Hence the $1$-nullity~\eqref{eq:curvature_constancy} is a parallel subbundle of $TM$. Since $\scrC_1(T_pM)
eq \{0\}$ because of Lemma~ef{le:curvature_constancy}, it is non-trivial and thus $\scrC_1(TM) = TM$ by the irreducibility of $M$. This implies that $M$ has constant sectional curvature, in particular the holonomy group is $\SO(n)$ which acts transitively on the unit sphere of $T_pM$. But this is contrary to our assumptions. So far we have shown that $\cyclic_{xyz}
abla_x\kappa(y,z)|_p = 0$ at all points $p$ of $M$ where $\d \, 	race \, \kappa|_p 
eq 0$ or $	race \, \kappa$ is constant on an open neighbourhood of $p$. Obviously the set of these points is dense in $M$. Since moreover the set points where the cyclic sum $\cyclic_{xyz}
abla_x\kappa(y,z)$ vanishes is closed, we conclude that $\kappa$ is Killing. We finish the proof of~(a) of Proposition~ef{p:get_rid} by showing that automatically $\kappa = \kappa^C$: we use~\eqref{eq:Ricci_spur_von_C_1} and~\eqref{eq:vergleich_der_spur_von_kappa_mit_der_skalaren_kruemmung_von_C} to obtain that  egin{align*} \widetilde \Ric^C(x,y) \stackrel{\eqref{eq:def_modified_Ricci_trace_und_tilde_scalC}}{=} \Ric^C(x,y) +  rac{1}{4} 
abla^2_{x,y}\scal^C \stackrel{\eqref{eq:Ricci_spur_von_C_1},\eqref{eq:vergleich_der_spur_von_kappa_mit_der_skalaren_kruemmung_von_C}}{=} 2  ig (\langle x,yangle 	race \, \kappa - \kappa(x,y) ig ). \end{align*} Hence  egin{equation*} \widetilde\scal^C\;\;=\;\;2(n - 1)	race \, \kappa. \end{equation*} Inserting the previous into~\eqref{eq:def_kappaC} shows that $\kappa = \kappa^C$. This finishes the proof of Part~(a) of Proposition~ef{p:get_rid}.

