onumber\ &\le (1+m^{1- rac{1}{r}})2^{- rac{m}{20r}} \Big(\sum_{j\in\Z}\|f*\check{\phi}_{m+j}\|_{2r}^r\|g*\check{\phi}_{\gamma,m,j}\|_{2r}^r\Big)^ rac{1}{r}. \end{align} Notice that for $r\in [1,\infty)$ and for any $f, \phi\in\s(\R)$, we have  egin{align*} \Big(\sum_{j\in\Z}\|f*\phi_j\|_{2r}^{2r}\Big)^ rac{1}{2r}&\le \Bigg(\int_\R \sum_{j\in\Z}|(f*\phi_j)(x)|^{2r}dx\Bigg)^ rac{1}{2r}\ &\le \Bigg(\int_\R \Bigg(\sum_{j\in\Z}|(f*\phi_j)(x)|^2\Bigg)^rdx\Bigg)^ rac{1}{2r} = \Bigg(\int_\R \Bigg\{ igg(\sum_{j\in\Z}|(f*\phi_j)(x)|^2 igg)^ rac{1}{2}\Bigg\}^{2r}dx\Bigg)^ rac{1}{2r}\ &=\Bigg\| igg(\sum_{j\in\Z}|f*\phi_j(x)|^2 igg)^ rac{1}{2}\Bigg\|_{2r} \lesssim \|f\|_{2r}, \end{align*} here for the last relation we used standard Littlewood-Paley theory. By Cauchy Schwartz, the hypothesis on $\g\in \NF$ and the result above, we obtain  egin{align} \Big(\sum_{j\in\Z}\|f*\check{\phi}_{m+j}\|_{2r}^r\|g*\check{\phi}_{\gamma,m,j}\|_{2r}^r\Big)^ rac{1}{r}&\le \Big(\sum_{j\in\Z}\|f*\check{\phi}_{m+j}\|_{2r}^{2r}\Big)^ rac{1}{2r}\Big(\sum_{j\in\Z}\|g*\check{\phi}_{\gamma,m,j}\|_{2r}^{2r}\Big)^ rac{1}{2r} 
