The following inequality holds for an $(n,K,\varepsilon)$ LOCC-assisted secret key agreement protocol over a multiplex channel $\mc{N}$:  egin{equation} F(\omega_{\vv{SK}},\gamma_{\vv{SK}})\geq 1-\varepsilon. \end{equation} For any $\sigma_{\vv{SK}}\in\FS(:\vv{SK}:)$, we have following bound due to inequality \eqref{eq:fid-conv-proof} and Theorem~ef{thm:priv-gme}:  egin{equation} \log_2 K\leq D^\varepsilon_h(\omega_{\vv{SK}}\Vert\sigma_{\vv{SK}}). \end{equation} Employing inequality \eqref{eq:hyp-sand-rel} in the limit $\alpha	o+\infty$, we obtain  egin{align} \log_2 K &\leq D^\varepsilon_h(\omega_{\vv{SK}}\Vert\sigma_{\vv{SK}}) \ &\leq D_{\max}(\omega_{\vv{SK}}\Vert\sigma_{\vv{SK}})+\log_2\left( rac{1}{1-\varepsilon}ight). \end{align} Above inequality holds for arbitrary $\sigma\in\FS(:\vv{SK}:)$, therefore  egin{equation} \log_2 K \leq E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{SK}:)_{\omega}+\log_2\left( rac{1}{1-\varepsilon}ight), \end{equation} where $E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{SK}:)_{\omega}$ is the max-relative entropy of entanglement of the state $\omega_{\vv{SK}}$. The max-relative entropy of entanglement $E_{\max,\E}$ of a state is monotonically non-increasing under the action of LOCC channels and it is zero for states that are fully separable. Using these facts, we get that  egin{align} & E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{SK}:)_{\omega}
onumber \ &\leq E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(n)}A^{(n)}}:\vv{R^{(n)}}:\vv{P^{(n)}C^{(n)}}:)_{	au_n} \ &= E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(n)}A^{(n)}}:\vv{R^{(n)}}:\vv{P^{(n)}C^{(n)}}:)_{	au_n} 
onumber\ &\qquad - E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(1)}A^{(1)'}}:\vv{R^{(1)}B^{(1)}}:\vv{P^{(1)}}:)_{ho_1}\ &=E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(n)}A^{(n)}}:\vv{R^{(n)}}:\vv{P^{(n)}C^{(n)}}:)_{	au_n} 
onumber\ &\qquad +\left[\sum_{i=2}^n E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(i)}A^{(i)'}}:\vv{R^{(i)}B^{(i)}}:\vv{P^{(i)}}:)_{ho_{i}} ight.
onumber \ &\qquad -\left. \sum_{i=2}^n E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(i)}A^{(i)'}}:\vv{R^{(i)}B^{(i)}}:\vv{P^{(i)}}:)_{ho_{i}} ight]
onumber \ &\qquad - E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(1)}A^{(1)'}}:\vv{R^{(1)}B^{(1)}}:\vv{P^{(1)}}:)_{ho_{1}}\ & \leq \sum_{i=1}^n \left[ E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(i)}A^{(i)}}:\vv{R^{(i)}}:\vv{P^{(i)}C^{(i)}}:)_{	au_{i}} ight. 
onumber\ &\qquad -\left. E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(i)}A^{(i)'}}:\vv{R^{(i)}B^{(i)}}:\vv{P^{(i)}}:)_{ho_{i}} ight]\ &\leq n E_{\max,\E}(\mc{N}). \end{align} The first equality follows because $E_{\max,\E}(:\vv{L^{(1)}A^{(1)'}}:\vv{R^{(1)}B^{(1)}}:\vv{P^{(1)}}:)_{ho_{1}}=0$. The second inequality follows because $E_{\max,\GE}$ is monotone under LOCC channels and $ho_{i}=\mc{L}^{i}(	au_{i-1})$ for all $i\in\{2,3,\ldots,n\}$. The final inequality follows from Lemma~ef{lem:max-amor}. From inequalities \eqref{eq:con-max-proof} and \eqref{eq:amor-proof}, we conclude that  egin{equation} \log_2K\leq nE_{\max,\E}(\mc{N})+\log_2\left( rac{1}{1-\varepsilon}ight). \end{equation}

